  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9027734d34a03bb43947e2332bd51243, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Dear young owner,


    My niece showed me the reviews of your little
    restaurant on her phone. A countryside shop serving food from six countries?
    I had to write.


    I''m Malai. I''ve run a kitchen in Bangkok for thirty years,
    but I started at my mother''s dessert cart. Mango sticky rice was what children
    begged for, and what tired mothers bought to say "you did well today."


    Steam
    the sticky rice until it shines, pour warm coconut cream over it, and let it
    rest. Slice the mango just before serving.


    Sweet things are a small kindness.
    Give them often.'
